(FUN-19 — the shadowing rule applies to `value` too, and its runtime type
 tag travels with its payload. `retag slot` stores a TEXT into a global
 declared holding a NUMBER; `report slot` (a different function) then
 prints `seven`, so both halves of the pair were written to the global.
 `shadow slot` declares a local `slot`, prints 42, and leaves the global
 alone — the final `report slot` still prints `seven`.
 Also covers: FUN-20 (a mutation inside one function is visible to another
 only when it is genuinely the same global).
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox FUN-19.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   7
   seven
   42
   seven
)
a value called slot is 7.

To 'retag slot'.
  Set slot to "seven".

To 'report slot'.
  Print slot.

To 'shadow slot'.
  a value called slot is 42.
  Print slot.

